      "In UM a principal building that existed before the district was adopted may be converted into any use permitted there (255-120A(41))",
      "In OR an office may include one dwelling unit in the same building, by special exception (255-51A, Ord. No. 2460, 2025)",
      "Every principal building must have public water and sewer. A dwelling without both needs a one-acre lot (255-194)",
      "Detached garage or carport: at most 20 ft high and 30 by 30 ft, not in a required front yard or an accessory setback, 8 ft from a street line. Sheds and other accessory buildings: 12 ft (255-200D(12)(b), (c)). In R-5 no accessory structure may stand between the house and the street (255-47B(1))",
      "Parking: 1 space per dwelling unit with one bedroom or less, 2 with two or more bedrooms (255-204A)",
      "One recreational vehicle may be lived in as a temporary accessory residence for seven days once a year (255-200D(10)(e))",
      "In C-5 a building of more than 10,000 sq ft that existed when the district was adopted may be converted into apartments by special exception (255-92B). Not a path for a house"
